---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Changelog — Logchef" description="Logchef release notes and version history: VictoriaLogs, dashboards, live tail, the CLI, and every change, version by version." activeNav="changelog">
  <style>
    .cl-wrap { position: relative; overflow: clip; }
    .cl-wrap .bg-glow {
      width: min(900px, 120vw); height: min(900px, 120vw);
      top: -44%; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%);
    }
    main { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 8rem 1.5rem 4rem; }

    .page-header { margin-bottom: 3rem; padding-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
    .page-header .kicker { display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .page-header h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.4vw, 2.75rem); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.033em; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    .page-header p { color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: 1.0625rem; }

    .version { margin-bottom: 3rem; padding-bottom: 2.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); scroll-margin-top: 6rem; }
    .version:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
    /* The milestone release gets a blue-bordered frame, not a gradient wash —
       blue is the workspace colour and it should carry the emphasis alone. */
    .version.milestone {
      margin-inline: -1.25rem; padding: 1.75rem 1.25rem 2.5rem;
      border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 34%, var(--color-border));
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: var(--color-surface);
    }
    .version-header { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .version-tag { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 1.1875rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--color-text); }
    .version-tag.unreleased { color: var(--color-purple); }
    a.version-tag { text-decoration: none; }
    a.version-tag:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }
    .version-date {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--color-text-muted);
      background: var(--color-bg); border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
      padding: 0.25rem 0.625rem; border-radius: 5px;
    }
    .version-badge {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 500;
      text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      padding: 0.25rem 0.55rem; border-radius: 5px;
      border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-success) 40%, transparent);
      color: var(--color-success);
    }
    .version-link { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-left: auto; }
    .version-link:hover { color: var(--color-accent); text-decoration: none; }

    .change-section { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .change-section:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    /* Change types read as outlined mono chips — same family as the film's
       source chips, so severity stays legible without coloured blocks. */
    .change-type {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem;
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 500;
      text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      padding: 0.28rem 0.6rem; border-radius: 5px; margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
      border: 1px solid currentColor;
    }
    .change-type.added { color: var(--color-success); }
    .change-type.changed { color: var(--color-warning); }
    .change-type.fixed { color: var(--color-accent-soft); }
    .change-type.removed { color: var(--color-error); }
    .change-type.security { color: var(--color-purple); }
    .change-type.breaking { color: var(--color-warning); }
    .change-type svg { width: 12px; height: 12px; }

    .release-kicker {
      margin-bottom: 0.85rem; color: var(--color-accent-soft); font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    .release-intro { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.7; }
    .release-intro strong { color: var(--color-text); }
    .release-highlights {
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.75rem;
      margin: 0 0 2rem; padding: 0; list-style: none;
    }
    .release-highlights li {
      padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 8px;
      background: var(--color-bg);
      color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .release-highlights strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; color: var(--color-text); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
    .upgrade-note {
      margin: 0 0 1.75rem; padding: 1rem 1.125rem;
      border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-warning) 32%, var(--color-border));
      border-left-width: 2px; border-left-color: var(--color-warning);
      border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
      background: var(--color-bg);
      color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.65;
    }
    .upgrade-note strong { color: var(--color-text); }
    .upgrade-note code {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8125rem;
      background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
      padding: 0.1em 0.35em; border-radius: 4px; color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .change-list { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.7rem; padding-left: 0.25rem; }
    .change-list li {
      position: relative; padding-left: 1.35rem;
      font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.65;
    }
    /* A short log line rather than a bullet — the mark's motif at list scale. */
    .change-list li::before {
      content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.7rem;
      width: 9px; height: 2px; border-radius: 1px;
      background: var(--color-accent); opacity: 0.65;
    }
    .change-list li strong { color: var(--color-text); font-weight: 500; }
    .change-list li code {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8125rem;
      background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
      padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
      border-radius: 4px; color: var(--color-accent-soft);
    }
    .change-list .breaking { color: var(--color-warning); font-weight: 600; }

    .contributors {
      margin-top: 1.25rem; padding-top: 1rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
      font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-text-muted);
    }
    .contributors a { color: var(--color-text-secondary); }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      main { padding-top: 6.5rem; }
      .version-header { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.5rem; }
      .version-link { margin-left: 0; }
      .version.milestone { margin-inline: -0.75rem; padding-inline: 0.9rem; }
      .release-highlights { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
  </style>

  <div class="cl-wrap">
  <div class="bg-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <main>
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="kicker">Release history</span>
      <h1>Changelog</h1>
      <p>What's new in Logchef.</p>
    </header>

    <!-- v2.0.0 -->
    <article class="version milestone" id="v2.0.0">
      <div class="version-header">
        <a class="version-tag" href="#v2.0.0">v2.0.0</a>
        <span class="version-date">Aug 8, 2026</span>
        <span class="version-badge">Latest</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/mr-karan/logchef/releases/tag/v2.0.0" class="version-link" target="_blank">Release notes &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <p class="release-kicker">A new chapter for Logchef</p>
      <p class="release-intro">
        <strong>Logchef 2.0 is the largest release in the project's history.</strong> It grows Logchef from a ClickHouse log explorer into a multi-datasource log exploration platform. VictoriaLogs now sits beside ClickHouse as a first-class datasource, while dashboards, live tail, local authentication, query history, usage analytics, and a substantially more capable CLI turn Logchef into a complete place to investigate and understand logs.
      </p>

      <ul class="release-highlights">
        <li><strong>VictoriaLogs, end to end</strong>Explore with LogchefQL or LogsQL, inspect fields, build dashboards and alerts, generate queries with AI, and tail logs live.</li>
        <li><strong>Dashboards, brand new</strong>Build operational views from log queries. Drag, resize, and preview panels on the grid. Mix time series, stats, tables, horizontal bars, and donut breakdowns.</li>
        <li><strong>Live logs everywhere</strong>Follow matching rows from either backend in the web explorer or terminal, with server-side stream guardrails.</li>
        <li><strong>Deploy your way</strong>Use built-in email and password login with no OIDC dependency, or automatically provision approved users through SSO.</li>
        <li><strong>Investigation memory</strong>Return to your own query history; administrators can see recent activity and all-time usage trends by user and source.</li>
        <li><strong>CLI v0.2.1</strong>Query both backends, tail, explain, graph histograms, inspect fields, diagnose setup, and jump from the shell into the web explorer.</li>
      </ul>

      <aside class="upgrade-note">
        <strong>Before upgrading:</strong> if you provision sources with <code>provisioning.toml</code>, move each source's connection fields under <code>[sources.connection]</code> and add its <code>source_type</code>. Logchef exits with a migration hint if it finds the old flat format. Database migrations remain automatic. <a href="#v2-breaking">See the exact change &darr;</a>
      </aside>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type added">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
          Added
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>VictoriaLogs datasource</strong>: Connect with no auth, basic auth, or a bearer token; optionally set multi-tenant account/project IDs and an immutable server-side scope. Query it with LogchefQL or native LogsQL across the explorer, dashboards, alerts, field inspection, AI generation, and live tail. Log context and exports remain ClickHouse-only. <a href="/tutorials/victorialogs/">VictoriaLogs guide &rarr;</a></li>
          <li><strong>Built-in local authentication</strong>: Run Logchef with email and password accounts, alongside OIDC or without an external identity provider. The configured bootstrap admin can be rotated on restart, and local login attempts are limited by IP and email. <a href="/getting-started/configuration/#local-authentication-run-without-oidc">Local authentication &rarr;</a></li>
          <li><strong>Automatic SSO provisioning</strong>: Allow first-time OIDC users from approved email domains to create a regular account and join configured default teams. <a href="/getting-started/configuration/#sso-auto-provisioning-jit-user-creation">SSO auto-provisioning &rarr;</a></li>
          <li><strong>Live tail</strong>: Flip on Live to stream matching rows as they arrive. ClickHouse uses efficient polling; VictoriaLogs proxies its native stream. Session, concurrency, and rows-per-second limits keep a shared instance bounded.</li>
          <li><strong>Dashboards</strong>: A brand-new module for operational views, mixing ClickHouse and VictoriaLogs panels on one grid. Move and resize panels directly on the canvas, then edit them in a full-height drawer with a live query preview.</li>
          <li><strong>More ways to visualize logs</strong>: Time-series panels support line, area, grouped bar, or stacked bar charts. Category breakdowns render as horizontal bars or donut charts alongside stat and table panels.</li>
          <li><strong>Dashboard result cache</strong>: Per-dashboard TTL caching reuses panel results across viewers and refreshes, reducing repeated backend work without caching ad-hoc explorer queries.</li>
          <li><strong>Query history and usage analytics</strong>: Reopen your recent queries in the explorer or with <code>logchef history</code>. Administrators get recent Query Activity plus durable all-time trends by source and user.</li>
          <li><strong>AI for every supported query mode</strong>: Generate and validate LogchefQL, ClickHouse SQL, or LogsQL, with one automatic repair attempt for recognized syntax errors. AWS Bedrock joins OpenAI-compatible providers.</li>
          <li><strong>Per-source ClickHouse guardrails</strong>: Cap execution time, result/read rows and bytes, set read-only mode, and choose overflow behavior for each shared ClickHouse source.</li>
          <li><strong>Client-side column filters</strong>: Narrow loaded rows from a column header with text matching or numeric comparisons, without issuing another query.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type changed">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 20v-8m0 0V4m0 8h8m-8 0H4"/></svg>
          Changed
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>Datasource-neutral architecture</strong>: Source configuration, query compilation, execution, inspection, and UI feature gates now flow through provider capabilities instead of ClickHouse-specific assumptions.</li>
          <li><strong>Large ClickHouse results stream progressively</strong>: Preview responses no longer buffer the complete result in server memory before returning it.</li>
          <li><strong>Credentials stay private</strong>: APIs return whether a credential exists, never the stored secret; leaving it blank while editing preserves the current value.</li>
          <li><strong>Cleaner, timezone-correct charts</strong>: Sparse histograms fill missing buckets with zero, grouped series keep exact totals, and dashboard time ranges align to the viewer's timezone.</li>
          <li><strong>Source Stats loads predictably</strong>: Metadata and bounded recent activity load and refresh independently, so slow activity queries do not block the whole page.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type security">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 3l7 4v5c0 4.5-2.9 7.6-7 9-4.1-1.4-7-4.5-7-9V7l7-4z"/></svg>
          Security &amp; reliability
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>Safe dashboard sharing and editing</strong>: Stored tooltip XSS is closed, concurrent saves detect conflicts, corrupt panels are isolated, and viewers only receive panels backed by sources they can access.</li>
          <li><strong>Hardened VictoriaLogs connections</strong>: Auth and tenant headers cannot be overridden, stale credentials are cleared when auth changes, health checks exercise the real query path, and slow request paths have read deadlines.</li>
          <li><strong>Request and proxy controls</strong>: Opt-in login/query rate limits and trusted-proxy client-IP resolution protect public or shared deployments without trusting spoofable forwarding headers.</li>
          <li><strong>Session lifecycle fixes</strong>: Deleting a user revokes their sessions immediately, and expired sessions are swept in the background.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type fixed">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
          Notable fixes
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>Condition alerts aggregate the selected field</strong> for <code>sum</code>, <code>avg</code>, <code>min</code>, and <code>max</code>, on both backends.</li>
          <li><strong>Alert evaluation keeps ClickHouse column metadata</strong>, fixing successful queries that previously failed only on the alert path.</li>
          <li><strong>Saved-query and URL modes stay consistent</strong>: LogchefQL, ClickHouse SQL, and LogsQL are validated appropriately, and drafts no longer leak LogchefQL into native mode.</li>
          <li><strong>Unsupported exports fail clearly</strong>: Sources without export capability hide Download and return a clean <code>400</code>, rather than starting a doomed job.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="change-section" id="v2-breaking">
        <div class="change-type breaking">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 9v4m0 4h.01M10.3 4.2L2.7 17.4A2 2 0 004.4 20h15.2a2 2 0 001.7-2.6L13.7 4.2a2 2 0 00-3.4 0z"/></svg>
          Breaking change
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>Provisioned source shape</strong>: Every <code>[[sources]]</code> entry now needs <code>source_type = "clickhouse"</code> or <code>"victorialogs"</code>, with provider-specific fields nested under <code>[sources.connection]</code>. Teams, members, descriptions, retention, and metadata-field settings are unchanged. <a href="/getting-started/provisioning/">Migration example &rarr;</a></li>
          <li><strong>Metadata migrations</strong>: SQLite migrations 000025–000032 and Postgres migrations 000002–000007 add datasource-neutral sources, local-auth credentials, dashboards, case-insensitive emails, query history, and durable daily usage stats. They apply automatically; case-only duplicate emails must be resolved manually if detected.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- CLI v0.2.1 -->
    <article class="version" id="cli-v0.2.1">
      <div class="version-header">
        <a class="version-tag" href="#cli-v0.2.1">CLI v0.2.1</a>
        <span class="version-date">Jul 21, 2026</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/mr-karan/logchef/releases/tag/cli-v0.2.1" class="version-link" target="_blank">Release notes &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
        A polished companion to the v2 server and the feature-packed CLI v0.2.0 release: interactive sessions now show the installed version in a Logchef banner and unobtrusively report when a newer stable CLI is available. Both can be disabled for scripts, CI, or quieter terminals.
      </p>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type added">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
          Added
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>Startup banner</strong>: Interactive runs identify the current CLI version; disable it in config, with an environment variable, in CI, or with <code>--quiet</code>.</li>
          <li><strong>Update notification</strong>: A cached version check announces newer stable releases without slowing every invocation, with the same opt-out controls.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- v2.0.0-alpha.1 -->
    <article class="version" id="v2.0.0-alpha.1">
      <div class="version-header">
        <a class="version-tag" href="#v2.0.0-alpha.1">v2.0.0-alpha.1</a>
        <span class="version-date">Jul 20, 2026</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/mr-karan/logchef/releases/tag/v2.0.0-alpha.1" class="version-link" target="_blank">Release notes &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
        First public preview of the v2 architecture: VictoriaLogs as a datasource, live tail, local authentication, dashboards, query history, usage analytics, and the datasource-neutral provider layer. The stable v2.0.0 release above includes the completed feature set and hardening work.
      </p>
    </article>

    <!-- CLI v0.2.0 -->
    <article class="version" id="cli-v0.2.0">
      <div class="version-header">
        <a class="version-tag" href="#cli-v0.2.0">CLI v0.2.0</a>
        <span class="version-date">Jul 20, 2026</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/mr-karan/logchef/releases/tag/cli-v0.2.0" class="version-link" target="_blank">Release notes &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
        The command-line tool catches up with the v2.0 server. It now queries VictoriaLogs sources the same way it queries ClickHouse, follows logs live in your terminal, and adds a handful of commands for exploring and debugging without leaving the shell.
      </p>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type added">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
          Added
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>VictoriaLogs support</strong>: Query your VictoriaLogs sources from the terminal, just like ClickHouse ones.</li>
          <li><strong>Live tail in the terminal</strong>: <code>logchef tail</code> now follows matching logs as they arrive, on ClickHouse and VictoriaLogs.</li>
          <li><strong>Jump to the web explorer</strong>: <code>logchef open</code> opens your current query in the browser, with the query and time range already filled in.</li>
          <li><strong>See the query first</strong>: <code>logchef explain</code> prints the query Logchef would run, without running it.</li>
          <li><strong>Counts over time</strong>: <code>logchef histogram</code> shows how often something happens across a time range.</li>
          <li><strong>Find your fields</strong>: <code>logchef fields</code> lists a source's fields and their common values, so you know what to filter on.</li>
          <li><strong>Your recent queries</strong>: <code>logchef history</code> reopens queries you ran earlier.</li>
          <li><strong>Check your setup</strong>: <code>logchef doctor</code> diagnoses server, auth, and source problems when something isn't working.</li>
          <li><strong>Shell completions</strong>: <code>logchef completions</code> for bash, zsh, and fish.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- v1.7.0 -->
    <article class="version" id="v1.7.0">
      <div class="version-header">
        <a class="version-tag" href="#v1.7.0">v1.7.0</a>
        <span class="version-date">Jul 6, 2026</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/mr-karan/logchef/releases/tag/v1.7.0" class="version-link" target="_blank">Release notes &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
        Logchef 1.7 makes the metadata store <strong>pluggable</strong>. Alongside the default single-binary SQLite, you can now run an <strong>opt-in Postgres backend</strong> so multiple Logchef replicas share state behind a load balancer. That's the groundwork for high availability. SQLite stays the default, so single-instance setups are unchanged. The release also lets you <strong>switch alerting off</strong> server-wide, opens <strong>collection curation</strong> to any participant, adds an admin <strong>"All Queries"</strong> browse view, and brings <strong>type-to-filter pickers and searchable, sortable tables</strong> to the member and resource pages.
      </p>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type added">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
          Added
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>Opt-in Postgres metadata backend</strong>: Store users, teams, sources, saved queries, collections, alerts, tokens, and settings in Postgres instead of SQLite, so several Logchef replicas can serve any request off shared state. Set <code>database.driver = "postgres"</code> with a <code>[postgres]</code> DSN (or the matching env vars). SQLite remains the default and the single-binary start is unchanged; your logs always stay in ClickHouse. <a href="/operations/database-backends/">Database backends &amp; HA &rarr;</a></li>
          <li><strong>Turn alerting off server-wide</strong>: Set <code>alerts.enabled = false</code> and the UI hides alerting entirely while every alert endpoint returns a clean <code>503</code>. Useful when you run Logchef purely for exploration, or want a single alert-evaluating instance.</li>
          <li><strong>"All Queries" browse for admins</strong>: Global admins can now see every saved query, including ones not pinned to any collection. Queries on sources you can't reach show as locked.</li>
          <li><strong>Redesigned Library</strong>: Saved queries and collections merge into a single <code>/logs/library</code> (collections rail + detail pane). Collections gain an <strong>editor</strong> role, and editing a saved query is delegated to its creator, a global admin, or an owner/editor of a shared collection that contains it. The Save dialog gets an inline collection picker, and the UI only offers Edit/Delete actions you're actually allowed to take.</li>
          <li><strong>Curate shared collections as a member</strong>: Any participant (owner, editor, or member) can pin, move, and remove queries in a shared collection. Renaming, deleting, and managing members stays owner-only.</li>
          <li><strong>Collection detail upgrades</strong>: Pin an existing saved query with an "Add query" search picker, move a query to another collection, and see each query's author in a new "Created by" column.</li>
          <li><strong>Searchable pickers &amp; tables</strong>: Type-to-filter dropdowns for inviting collection members and adding service accounts to teams, plus a search box and sortable columns on Manage Sources and team-member lists.</li>
          <li><strong>Token expiry everywhere</strong>: The service-tokens admin page now shows the same expiry status as the profile API-token list (never expires / expires / expiring soon / expired), and the CLI flags an expired saved token in <code>logchef auth current</code>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type changed">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 20v-8m0 0V4m0 8h8m-8 0H4"/></svg>
          Changed
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>Pluggable store architecture</strong>: The metadata layer now sits behind a backend-agnostic contract with a shared conformance suite that runs against both SQLite and Postgres in CI, so the two backends stay in lockstep.</li>
          <li><strong>Upgraded to Go 1.26</strong> with hot-path optimizations across query handling.</li>
          <li><strong>Collection member list is owner-only</strong>: now enforced on the server, not just hidden in the UI.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type fixed">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
          Fixed
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>Inline permission errors show a toast</strong> instead of bouncing you to a full-page Forbidden view. Toggles, saves, and deletes stay put on a 403.</li>
          <li><strong>Dead toggles work again</strong>: several Switch/Checkbox controls (admin Active toggle, alert enable/disable, source TLS/auth, column selector, variable multi-selects) were silently no-op'd by a binding mismatch and now respond.</li>
          <li><strong>Saved-query resolver no longer crashes</strong> on certain resolve paths; it returns a clean error instead.</li>
          <li><strong>Accurate access errors</strong> for exports and shared queries: <code>404</code> only when something's missing, <code>403</code> when you lack team access.</li>
          <li><strong>Tighter memory accounting</strong> on large responses (fixes an under-count from the performance pass), cancellable field-value loading, and identifier validation on provisioned sources.</li>
          <li><strong>UI polish</strong>: the add-query dialog no longer overflows, the Library "All queries" view survives navigation, and the date picker's type drift is fixed (TypeScript checks are green and enforced in CI again).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- v1.6.1 -->
    <article class="version" id="v1.6.1">
      <div class="version-header">
        <a class="version-tag" href="#v1.6.1">v1.6.1</a>
        <span class="version-date">May 20, 2026</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/mr-karan/logchef/releases/tag/v1.6.1" class="version-link" target="_blank">Release notes &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
        Patch release. Adds <strong>Service accounts</strong>: non-login principals you can add to teams and issue scoped API tokens for. Every token now carries an explicit scope list (e.g. <code>logs:read</code>, <code>alerts:write</code>) enforced by middleware, with presets and an active-preset highlight in the picker. The team member dialog distinguishes humans from service accounts, and service principals get a clear badge in team rosters. Also surfaces ClickHouse column comments through the schema API for the new Logchef CLI v0.1.6 to consume.
      </p>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type added">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
          Added
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>Service accounts</strong>: Non-login principals managed at <strong>Administration &rarr; Service Tokens</strong>. Cannot authenticate via OIDC or CLI exchange; exist only to own tokens and team memberships. <a href="/features/service-tokens/">Learn more &rarr;</a></li>
          <li><strong>Scoped API tokens</strong>: Tokens now carry an explicit list of scopes (<code>logs:read</code>, <code>alerts:write</code>, &hellip;). Presets in the picker: Read-only, Logs viewer, Logs analyst, Alerts manager, Source admin, Full access. The active preset stays highlighted while the selection matches.</li>
          <li><strong>Account-type toggle in Add Team Member</strong>: Pick Human user or Service account; the dropdown filters to that type and shows the principal's name with email as a subtitle instead of the raw service-account email.</li>
          <li><strong>Service account badge</strong> in team member tables: a bot icon and "Service account" pill so automation principals are visually distinct from humans.</li>
          <li><strong>Manage teams on each service account card</strong>: team chips, a destructive warning when an account is in zero teams (its tokens won't reach any source), and an in-place add/remove dialog.</li>
          <li><strong>Schema column descriptions</strong>: The schema API now surfaces ClickHouse column comments. Consumed by Logchef CLI v0.1.6's <code>schema</code> command.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type changed">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 20v-8m0 0V4m0 8h8m-8 0H4"/></svg>
          Changed
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>"Create API Token" defaults to the Read-only preset.</strong> Previously defaulted to Full access, which made the scope picker look entirely disabled out of the box.</li>
          <li><strong>Read-only preset is now every <code>:read</code> scope.</strong> Adds <code>tokens:read</code>, <code>users:read</code>, <code>settings:read</code>. Admin-gated routes still enforce admin role separately.</li>
          <li><strong><code>/admin/users/*</code> routes 404 on service accounts.</strong> Service principals are managed via the dedicated <code>/admin/service-accounts/*</code> path so they can't be promoted through the human-user CRUD path.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type fixed">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
          Fixed
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>Scope picker checkboxes are interactive again.</strong> The component was bound to <code>:checked</code>; the underlying primitive uses <code>model-value</code>. The bug was hidden behind the old Full-access default.</li>
          <li><strong>Token creation rejects empty scopes (HTTP 400).</strong> Requests with no scopes used to silently mint a full-access token.</li>
          <li><strong>Corrupt or empty stored scopes fail closed.</strong> A token row with malformed scope JSON now grants no access instead of full access.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- CLI v0.1.6 -->
    <article class="version" id="cli-v0.1.6">
      <div class="version-header">
        <a class="version-tag" href="#cli-v0.1.6">CLI v0.1.6</a>
        <span class="version-date">May 20, 2026</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/mr-karan/logchef/releases/tag/cli-v0.1.6" class="version-link" target="_blank">Release notes &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
        Major CLI release. Adds four new subcommands (<code>saved-queries</code>, <code>find</code>, <code>tail</code>, <code>whoami</code>, <code>auth current</code>), full time-range injection on raw SQL, agent-friendly output formats (<code>msg</code>, <code>json-flat</code>), a symmetric <code>--explain</code> / <code>--dry-run</code> split across <code>query</code> and <code>sql</code>, and TTY-aware highlighting so pipes don't need <code>--no-highlight</code>. Requires Logchef server v1.6.1+ for the saved-queries resolve endpoint and ClickHouse column descriptions.
      </p>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type added">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
          Added
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong><code>saved-queries</code></strong>: List and run saved queries by name, numeric ID, or a pasted explorer URL. <code>--var</code>, <code>--limit</code>, <code>--show-sql</code>, and all output-format overrides supported.</li>
          <li><strong><code>find &lt;pattern&gt;</code></strong>: Discover sources with recent matches for a service, job, host, or message pattern. Each match line is followed by per-column samples: label-shaped columns (service/host/job_name) get the top 3 values with counts; free-form text columns (msg) get one truncated sample row. Suppress with <code>--no-samples</code>. Per-source timeout defaults to 30s.</li>
          <li><strong><code>tail &lt;query&gt;</code></strong>: Follow matching LogchefQL rows by polling. <code>text</code>, <code>jsonl</code>, or <code>msg</code> output; stable dedup across column-order changes; one-shot stderr warning when a poll returns at <code>--limit</code>.</li>
          <li><strong><code>whoami</code></strong>: Print the authenticated user and accessible teams.</li>
          <li><strong><code>auth current</code></strong>: Offline subcommand that prints the active context, server URL, and token source (config vs env), plus the token expiry when it came from saved config. No network call. Useful for "is my <code>LOGCHEF_AUTH_TOKEN</code> even set?" diagnostics.</li>
          <li><strong>SQL time flags on <code>sql</code></strong>: <code>--since</code> / <code>--from</code> / <code>--to</code> inject a timestamp predicate before the first top-level <code>GROUP BY</code> / <code>ORDER BY</code> / <code>LIMIT</code> / <code>HAVING</code> / <code>SETTINGS</code> / <code>FORMAT</code>. The scanner skips string literals, quoted identifiers, comments, and parenthesized subqueries; use <code>__START__</code> / <code>__END__</code> placeholders for full control (e.g. CTEs).</li>
          <li><strong><code>--explain</code> / <code>--show-sql</code> on <code>query</code> and <code>sql</code></strong>: Print <code>Generated SQL: &lt;sql&gt;</code> to stderr, then continue executing. Plays cleanly with <code>--output jsonl | jq</code> pipes.</li>
          <li><strong><code>--dry-run</code> on <code>query</code> and <code>sql</code></strong>: Print the resolved SQL to stdout (no prefix) and exit without keeping results. <code>sql --dry-run</code> is fully offline; <code>query --dry-run</code> calls the server once for LogchefQL translation.</li>
          <li><strong><code>--output msg</code></strong>: Print only the message column (one row per line) on <code>query</code>, <code>sql</code>, <code>collections</code>, and <code>saved-queries</code>. Falls back to the first selected column when <code>msg</code> isn't projected.</li>
          <li><strong><code>--output json-flat</code></strong>: Hoist JSON-shaped <code>msg</code> fields to top-level JSON rows on <code>query</code>, <code>sql</code>, <code>collections</code>, and <code>saved-queries</code>.</li>
          <li><strong><code>LOGCHEF_DEFAULT_TEAM</code> / <code>LOGCHEF_DEFAULT_SOURCE</code></strong>: Env defaults when <code>--team</code> / <code>--source</code> are omitted. Precedence: flag &rarr; env &rarr; saved config.</li>
          <li><strong>Schema column descriptions</strong>: <code>schema --output text</code> shows a new DESCRIPTION column when the source's ClickHouse columns carry comments; <code>schema --output json</code> includes them inline.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type changed">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 20v-8m0 0V4m0 8h8m-8 0H4"/></svg>
          Changed
        </div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>Highlighting auto-disables on non-TTY output.</strong> All five subcommands (<code>query</code>, <code>sql</code>, <code>collections</code>, <code>saved-queries</code>, <code>tail</code>) skip ANSI escapes when stdout is piped, so <code>... | jq</code> and <code>... &gt; file</code> produce clean output without <code>--no-highlight</code>. The flag still works as an explicit override.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

